To 'show ends' of a list called items.
    Print "last: {items's last}".
    Print "first: {items's first}".
    Print items's last.
    Print element 2 of items.

To 'keep the first' of a list called items.
    a text called word is items's first.
    Print word.
    a list called gathered is [].
    append items's last to gathered.
    Print gathered.

a list called letters is ["b", "c"].
'show ends' of letters.
'keep the first' of letters.
a list called mixed is [1, "two", 3.5].
'show ends' of mixed.
a list called nested is [[1, 2], [3]].
'show ends' of nested.
a list called grown is [].
append "x" to grown.
append "y" to grown.
Print grown's first.
Print "{grown's last}".
a list called blank is [].
'show ends' of blank.
